  "2026-09-28T06:26:30.268Z",claude-hub,"2026-09-28: pinned pm-ops 2026.9.28 and re-copied its templates/prepare-merge-driver.ts (pm-ops#124: the omit-dev skip now checks every Node resolution path for an incomplete hoisted pm-ops, so a broken ancestor install fails instead of silently skipping the merge drivers). release:check and changelog:check pass on this branch."
  "2026-10-02T22:11:44.555Z",codex-sol,"Restart: current branch is already rebased on main; previous bot replies were inspected without repeating them. Greptile graph-export finding is an acknowledged security trade-off: GET/HEAD cannot run extension activation; pure export fidelity stays tracked in pm-web-38n5. Add a current graph regression receipt and run the unchanged full locked CI gate using PM_FLEET_ROOT. Existing coverage target and substantive reviews stay open; no Docker or hosted service changes."
  "2026-10-02T23:03:20.822Z",codex-sol,"Catalog fixes now yield 409/409 tests and unchanged configured coverage, but full gate fails production audit on transitive ip-address 10.5.0 via express-rate-limit ^10.2.0. GHSA-h3mg-xc3c-68pw affects <=10.7.0 and is patched >=10.7.1. Refresh only the transitive lockfile resolution within the existing range, retain all audit thresholds and SDK pins, reinstall reproducibly and rerun full locked gate. No hosted or telemetry/config changes."
  "2026-10-02T23:14:49.801Z",codex-sol,"Transitive lock refresh changed only ip-address 10.5.0 to 10.7.3; reproducible npm ci and production audit report zero vulnerabilities. Retry full gate was correctly refused by snapshot assertion because the new shell omitted required PM_FLEET_ROOT and scanned worktree inventory (408/409 tests). This is execution environment error, not a source/snapshot change: rerun unchanged full gate with explicit canonical fleet root. All assertions and prior failed receipts retained."
  "2026-10-02T23:21:58.634Z",codex-sol,"Final corrected-environment full gate passes: PM_FLEET_ROOT set to canonical fleet, locked release:check 409/409 tests, zero skips, 32-source coverage 84.39 lines / 80.48 branches / 77.82 functions, no independent statements metric. Doc/duplication gates, production audit zero vulnerabilities, real packed npm/Bun, changelog/date and attestation pass. ip-address lock-only 10.5.0 to 10.7.3 is the sole dependency delta, bounded malformed IPv6 rejection passes, and npm ci is reproducible. Accepted graph-fidelity tradeoff remains pm-web-38n5. Keep 100 percent coverage and substantive final-head review prerequisites open; no hosted deployment or user-data change. Release claim for orchestrator."
  "2026-10-02T23:39:05.567Z",codex-sol,"Cubic review corrections: title now lists all three tool pins. Correction to the 23:03 audit receipt: express-rate-limit is ^8.6.2 resolved 8.7.0; its transitive ip-address range is ^10.2.0, upgraded from 10.5.0 to 10.7.3. Preserve original history and append this accurate dependency-chain receipt. New teardown-order assertion will fail before fixing fixture cleanup; no runtime graph behavior change."
  "2026-10-02T23:45:37.860Z",codex-sol,"Second review round: actual teardown assertion failed under old t.after ordering, then passed after one cleanup hook closes the app before restoring both environment variables and removing the workspace. Linked real graph test passes. Four valid tracker findings are clarified without dropping dated notes/history; neighbors response parity remains explicitly unmet. Full unchanged gate is queued with canonical PM_FLEET_ROOT; pushing tested correction allows exact-head CI and bots to run concurrently. Do not treat pending full gate or reviews as approval."
  "2026-10-02T23:47:58.329Z",codex-sol,"Review gate caught prefer-const in deferred server binding before tests ran. Corrected with a constant fixture-state holder and constant local server; retain early after hook, shutdown-order assertions and fail-safe restoration. Direct eslint invocation correctly refused absent ambient config; use the repository canonical lint wrapper via the unchanged full gate. No lint rule/config changed. Rerun with canonical fleet root and retain failed receipts."
  "2026-10-02T23:52:52.285Z",codex-sol,"Third/final candidate: constant fixture holder passes canonical lint and full unchanged release:check with explicit canonical fleet root: 409/409, zero skips, configured 32-source L/B/F 84.39/80.48/77.82. Production audit zero vulnerabilities, npm/Bun packed acceptance, changelog/date and attestation pass. Actual teardown-order assertion failed before the single hook fix, and focused/linked graph tests pass afterward. Four Cubic tracker corrections preserve history and explicitly keep extension-native response parity unmet. Record final source/receipt together, release claim; remaining source-100-percent, parity, hosted and required-review gates are independent. Max three review rounds; no item closure or merge."
  "2026-10-04T09:37:18.792Z",pi-land-s2,"Audit-driven SDK pin bump: GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm (updated 2026-10-02) flags every braces release <=3.0.3 with no patched version, and pm-cli 2026.9.26's production fast-glob chain reached it, so npm audit --omit=dev reported 4 high findings and the full gate failed at audit:prod. pm-cli 2026.10.3/2026.10.4 replaced fast-glob with tinyglobby (no braces), so package.json and the lockfile now resolve @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.4 (the registry's audit-recommended fix) and manifest.json's extension floor matches it per the packaging gate. Nothing else changed: pm-changelog 2026.9.25 and pm-ops 2026.9.28 pins are untouched, no audit threshold or gate was weakened, and the full locked release:check with the canonical fleet root passes 409/409 tests with zero skips, production audit at zero vulnerabilities, coverage thresholds met, packed npm/Bun acceptance and changelog/date/attestation checks green. Title and acceptance criteria updated to name the pin this branch now certifies, matching the earlier reviewer precedent."
  "2026-10-04T13:44:22.815Z",codex-sol,"PR163 merged by orchestrator at13:42UTC (merge86c31b1); created certification branch from that new origin/main only. Reuse this existing open certification owner, exact required title, retain dated history. Absorb open Dependabot162/164/165/166, exact CodeQL v4.38.2 SHA2892aa5e19bbd11bc0cff5427e3b750a04d9e3c2 and latest npm pins. Upgrade ops/changelog10.4 and byte-copy published launcher; keep existing CLI/floor10.4. Full gate uses own disposable native PostgreSQL17.10 under sharedflock, noDocker/hosted/data/config changes. Existing whole-source ownerfy9a and privacy96 remain independent. Final rebase review metadata crossed orchestrator merge; cherry-picked own metadata commit into this consolidated PR and removed only the accidentally recreated remote branch under exact lease."
  "2026-10-04T13:45:57.475Z",codex-sol,"Latest exact tool/development pins installed, pg8.23.1 incorporates165, tsx4.23.15 incorporates162, types26.6.4 supersedes166; CodeQL exact SHA/comment from164 copied. Malformed lookup regression failed oldlauncher(ENOTDIR) then canonicaltemplate passes7/7. Managedpm-github10.4 installed with read-only repo dry-run; no scheduling or issue writes. Productionaudit0, fullaudit4high throughunpatchedbraces/fastglob/pmops; separatefollow-upcreated, no forcedbreakingoverride/downgrade. Keep unchanged fullgate and independentqualityownerfy9a; disposable nativePG fixture queued under sharedflock."
  "2026-10-04T13:52:56.405Z",codex-sol,"First full gate410tests failed408/410: workflow pin allowlist still named oldCodeQLSHA, and livefleetpm-ts-starter description nowSDK10.4. Updated exact allowlist from reviewedDependabotdiff; regenerated snapshot with npm run fleet:snapshot and canonicalPM_FLEET_ROOT (20extensions, registry reachable), preserved every catalog/source gate; focusedworkflow+catalog15/15pass. Mandatory packed acceptance exposed projectcreation500 beneathcopiedancestortracker. Installedtarball diagnostic reproduces CLI ancestor-init refusal; actualCLI regression failsoldimplementation. Fix explicitly initializes childworkspace with prefix and noninteractive defaults, preservesancestor settingsbytes. No --force/bypassedguard, no upstream defect claimed; repeat scoped/full/packed gates."
